// W6-03 U4a/t, S-82, S-783 (§8.1: "`rt` でない関数では、効果行への追加（署名への挿入）を修正候補に示し"; §18.1: a candidate leaves no error of its stage or an earlier one): the error is at the first use (the
// name `b`, on the line of the `let`), and the candidate that inserts ` uses {Alloc}` into the signature removes it: the file after the candidate has no error (`clean = true`; the check applies the candidate
// and looks again). The file has one function that has a candidate, as `clean` needs. The place of the candidate's edit is the signature of `k`, though the diagnostic is in the body.

pub fn k(n: U32) -> U32 uses {Alloc} {
  let x = n + 1
  let b: Buf[F32] = Buf.zeroed(x)   //~ E0601 @7
  b.len()
}
